C-DUP
-----
Li, Neupane, Paul, Song, Krishnamurthy, Roy Chowdhury, Swami.
"Stealthy Adversarial Perturbations Against Real-Time Video Classification Systems."
Network and Distributed System Security Symposium (NDSS), 2019.

Original implementation: https://github.com/sli057/Video-Perturbation  (TensorFlow 1.x)

`adapters/cdup_adapter.py` is a layer-by-layer PyTorch transcription of the authors'
generator (`generator_3D`) and training objective. No original source is included here.


U3D
---
Xie, Wang, Kong, Hong.
"Universal 3-Dimensional Perturbations for Black-Box Attacks on Video Recognition Systems."
IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy (S&P), 2022, pp. 1390-1407.

Reference implementation: https://github.com/alarst13/u3d
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 Al Arst.

`adapters/u3d_adapter.py` imports and drives that implementation **without modifying it**.
The code is not vendored in this repository; `scripts/setup_u3d.sh` fetches and builds it
under `repos/u3d/`.


Victim model
------------
MMAction2 C3D checkpoint (Sports-1M pretraining, fine-tuned on UCF-101 split-1).
`common/dfbench/victim.py` is a standalone re-implementation that runs without mmcv; its
logits were verified to match the original MMAction2 `Recognizer3D`.

C3D architecture: Tran, Bourdev, Fergus, Torresani, Paluri.
"Learning Spatiotemporal Features with 3D Convolutional Networks." ICCV, 2015.


PhantomSeal (deepfake target)
-----------------------------
Ren et al. "PhantomSeal: Proactive Deepfakes Defense with Identity/Context Protection and
Forensic Tracing." ACM CCS, 2026.

Implementation: https://github.com/LiangqinRen/PhantomSeal
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Liangqin Ren.

`deepfake/` imports PhantomSeal's code (SimSwap target, identity/context extractors, protection
objective, FaceNet-512 and dlib judges) without modifying it. PhantomSeal is not vendored in this
repository; it is cloned to `repos/PhantomSeal` (or `PHANTOMSEAL_ROOT`), and its setup script
downloads the third-party face-swapping projects, datasets and checkpoints, which remain under
their own licenses and terms.


